          <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-amber-100 dark:bg-amber-900/30 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5"><svg class="w-3 h-3 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 2l3.09 6.26L22 9.27l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 17.77l-6.18 3.25L7 14.14 2 9.27l6.91-1.01L12 2z"/></svg></span>
          <div><h3 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 text-sm mb-1">Resize in Your Slicer, Not the Tool</h3><p class="text-xs text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">The tool generates a model at a default scale. Resize it in your slicer (Cura, PrusaSlicer) to fit your printer bed and desired output size. This gives you millimeter-precise control over the final print dimensions.</p></div>
