    <section class="mt-16 sm:mt-20 border-t border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800 pt-14 sm:pt-16 scroll-mt-28 reveal" id="faq">
      <p class="section-tag">12 &mdash; FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="editorial-title mt-2 mb-8">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <dl class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl">
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">What is an STL file and why do I need one?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">STL (STereoLithography) is the universal file format for 3D printing. It represents a 3D surface as a mesh of triangles and is accepted by every 3D printer slicer, including Cura, PrusaSlicer, and Bambu Studio.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">Is this image to STL converter really free?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Yes, completely free. No registration, no hidden fees, no file count limits, no watermarks. All processing happens in your browser &mdash; there is no server to bill, so we keep it free forever.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">What image formats can I convert to STL?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">JPG, PNG, and SVG are fully supported with dedicated conversion modes. BMP, WebP, and other common raster formats also work through heightmap mode. SVG extrusion produces the best results for logos and icons.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">Where does my image go? Is it uploaded anywhere?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Nowhere. All processing happens entirely in your browser using JavaScript, Canvas, and WebGL APIs. Your images never leave your device. No data is ever uploaded to any server.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">What 3D file formats can I export to?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">You can export to STL (universal 3D printing), OBJ (Wavefront with color support for Blender), and GLB (modern glTF binary, ideal for web, AR, and VR). All formats generated in your browser.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">Can I use the generated STL for actual 3D printing?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Absolutely. The output is standard binary STL, ready for direct slicing in Cura, PrusaSlicer, Bambu Studio, or any other 3D printing software. No post-processing needed for most models.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">How is this different from server-based online converters?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Server-based converters upload your files to remote servers &mdash; privacy risk, size limits, wait times, daily caps. Our tool runs 100% in your browser &mdash; instant 3D preview, real-time adjustments, unlimited conversions, complete privacy.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">What conversion modes are available?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Three modes: Heightmap converts pixel brightness to 3D height for photo reliefs. SVG Extrusion extracts vector paths into solid 3D shapes for logos and text. Lithophane creates translucent panels that reveal an image when backlit.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">Does this work on mobile devices?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Yes, fully responsive. Upload photos from your phone, preview the 3D model with touch controls, and download STL files. Performance depends on device GPU.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">Do I need 3D modeling experience?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Not at all. This tool is designed for beginners. Upload an image, adjust a few sliders, download your STL. If you can take a photo, you can make a 3D model.</dd></div>
      
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">Is the STL output watertight and printable?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Yes. All three modes (heightmap, SVG extrusion, lithophane) produce manifold (watertight) meshes. The output passes standard mesh validation checks. You can slice and print immediately without mesh repair.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">What happens if I upload a very large image?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Images are automatically resized to 512px on the longest side before processing. This keeps conversion fast while maintaining more than enough detail for 3D printing. Original files up to 50MB are handled without issues since processing is local.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">Can I use the generated STL files for commercial purposes?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Yes. You own all STL files you generate. Use them for personal projects, sell them on Etsy or 3D model marketplaces, include them in commercial products, or share them freely. We claim no rights over your output.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">Why do some images produce better 3D results than others?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">The quality of the 3D relief depends heavily on the image's contrast and detail. Images with dramatic lighting, clear edges, and good tonal range produce the best results. Flat, low-contrast, or blurry images result in shallow, indistinct 3D surfaces. For best results, adjust your image's contrast in a photo editor before uploading.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">How does SVG extrusion handle complex designs?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">The SVG parser handles paths, polygons, rectangles, circles, ellipses, and compound shapes. Nested shapes create holes automatically. Complex designs with many elements may take slightly longer to triangulate but produce accurate results. If a design is too complex for extrusion, the tool auto-falls back to raster heightmap mode.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">What is the difference between Heightmap and Lithophane modes?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Heightmap mode creates a one-sided relief where brightness maps to height &mdash; ideal for viewing from the front. Lithophane mode creates a thin panel where thickness controls light transmission &mdash; designed to be backlit for viewing. Use heightmap for wall art and reliefs; use lithophane for lamps and light boxes.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">Does the tool work offline?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Once the page loads, the core conversion functionality works without an internet connection. The initial page load requires internet, but all image processing, 3D preview, and STL generation run entirely client-side with no network requests. You can convert images even if your connection drops after page load.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">How does the smoothness slider affect the STL output?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">Smoothness controls how much the mesh is simplified. Low smoothness preserves every pixel detail but creates larger STL files with more triangles. High smoothness produces simpler, smaller files but may lose fine texture. For detailed portraits, use low smoothness. For geometric shapes and logos, use higher smoothness for cleaner edges.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">Can I batch convert multiple images at once?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">The tool processes one image at a time. However, since all processing is local, you can convert images back-to-back with zero waiting. Many users keep the tool open and process a batch of photos sequentially. There is no queue, no daily limit, and no throttling.</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-1">Which 3D printing filament works best for photo reliefs?</dt><dd class="text-sm text-surface-500 leading-relaxed">For photo reliefs and decorative prints: PLA in any color works well. Matte PLA hides layer lines better. Silk/shiny PLA can make details harder to see. For lithophanes: white PLA or natural PLA is essential for proper light transmission. Avoid dark, transparent, or glitter filaments for lithophanes as they block or scatter light.</dd></div>
</dl>
